   "heading": "Save single table / Guardar una tabla",
   "segment_index": "S17.P1",
   "kind": "code_mismatch",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_presentation.qmd:517-517",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_presentation.es.qmd:514-514",
   "proposition": "The English says the display name passed to save_as_docx() is \"my table\" (two words, distinct from the flextable object my_table); the Spanish says the name is \"my_table\", which is the object name and does not match the code chunk beside it, which reads save_as_docx(\"my table\" = my_table, path = \"file.docx\").",
   "reader_consequence": "The Spanish reader loses the contrast the sentence is built on: passing the bare object versus passing a named argument whose name becomes the Word table title. Reading \"el nombre es my_table\", the reader looks for my_table in the chunk, finds only the object on the right-hand side, and can conclude the quoted title string is the object name, so writing their own call they may use the object name as the caption or omit the quoted name entirely.",
   "confidence": "high"
  }
